IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr1-interpretation`
IMPORT `cr1-part3-interpretation`
IMPORT `cr1-part3-outside-canada`

-- Tests of cr1-part3-interpretation.l4 (regulation 15) and cr1-part3-outside-canada.l4 (regulation 16). Every
-- expected value is written from the text (C.R.C.-c.-385.txt lines 221 to 260) before the run.

§ `Tests of regulations 15 and 16`

§§ `Regulation 15(1): employer operating in Canada`

-- Arguments: kind; included by regulation under 7(1)(e); has an establishment in Canada; subject to tax (or would be but for s 149); has taxable income.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `Her Majesty in right of Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `Her Majesty in right of a province` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `Her Majesty in right of a province` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (d): an establishment in Canada, liable to tax (or would be but for s 149), and taxable income for the year.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `another kind of employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `another kind of employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `another kind of employer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `another kind of employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A province whose employment was not brought in by regulation is still caught by (d) if it meets it.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` `Her Majesty in right of a province` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulation 15(1): employment in international transportation, establishment, ship; and 15(2)`

#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `a ship` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service by a person who is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `a freight or passenger train` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `another conveyance` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `a ship` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` `a ship` FALSE TRUE)

-- Arguments: in Canada; owned, leased or licensed by the employer; works or reports there; employees are paid from or at it.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `reg 15(1) — a craft is a ship` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — a craft is a ship` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1) — a craft is a ship` FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `reg 15(2) — the Part whose words and expressions Part III uses for the words it does not define` `the Regulations' Part III` EQUALS JUST `the Regulations' Part I`
#ASSERT `reg 15(2) — the Part whose words and expressions Part III uses for the words it does not define` `the Regulations' Part I` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 16: fixtures`

GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
`cr1 test employee abroad` facts MEANS `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada` WITH
    `ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS elem "reports" facts
    `resident in Canada` IS elem "resident" facts
    `paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS elem "paid" facts
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS elem "crown" facts
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS elem "province included" facts
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS elem "province agreement" facts
    `engaged outside Canada` IS elem "engaged outside" facts
    `engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS elem "services outside" facts
    `resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada` IS elem "resident prior" facts
    `in receipt of a representation allowance` IS elem "allowance" facts
    `performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act` IS elem "assistance" facts
    `resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced` IS elem "resident 3 months" facts
    `a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS elem "250(1)(b)" facts
    `living with the spouse or common-law partner` IS elem "living with" facts
    `resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada` IS elem "resident before" facts
    `the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS elem "treasury board" facts
    `the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS elem "province signifies" facts

§§ `Regulation 16(3) and 16(1)(a) to (d)`

#ASSERT `reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "engaged outside", "services outside"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "engaged outside")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "services outside")))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(a) — the employee ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "reports"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(a) — the employee ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` (`cr1 test employee abroad` EMPTY))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(b) — the employee is resident in Canada and paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "resident", "paid"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(b) — the employee is resident in Canada and paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "resident")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(b) — the employee is resident in Canada and paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "paid")))
-- (c): a Crown employee, not engaged locally, who was resident in Canada just before or receives a representation allowance.
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "resident prior"))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "allowance"))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "province included", "allowance"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "resident prior", "engaged outside", "services outside")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "resident prior", "allowance")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "province agreement", "allowance")))
-- (d): an international development assistance program, and residence in Canada in the three months before the services began.
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "assistance", "resident 3 months"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "assistance")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "resident 3 months")))

§§ `Regulation 16(1)(e) to (g)`

-- (e): the partner is described in (c) or (d) or in 250(1)(b); the employee lives with the partner, is a Crown (or agreement-province) employee, and was resident in Canada before.
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "resident prior")))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "assistance", "resident 3 months")))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)")))
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "province agreement", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)"))))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)"))))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)"))))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` EMPTY)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) NOTHING)
-- (f): a Crown employee engaged locally, and the President of the Treasury Board has said so.
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(f) — the Crown employee engaged locally is one the President of the Treasury Board wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "engaged outside", "services outside", "treasury board"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(f) — the Crown employee engaged locally is one the President of the Treasury Board wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "engaged outside", "services outside")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(f) — the Crown employee engaged locally is one the President of the Treasury Board wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "treasury board")))
-- (g): the same for a province that has an agreement and has signified.
#ASSERT `reg 16(1)(g) — the provincial employee engaged locally is one the province wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "province agreement", "engaged outside", "services outside", "province signifies"))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(g) — the provincial employee engaged locally is one the province wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "province agreement", "engaged outside", "services outside")))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1)(g) — the provincial employee engaged locally is one the province wishes included` (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "crown", "engaged outside", "services outside", "province signifies")))

§§ `Regulation 16(1) as a whole`

#ASSERT `reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "reports")) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "reports")) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "reports")) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "reports")) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`cr1 test employee abroad` EMPTY) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "living with", "crown", "resident before")) (JUST (`cr1 test employee abroad` (LIST "250(1)(b)")))

§§ `Regulation 16(2)`

-- Arguments: in another country; described in (1) or in international transportation; the employer operates in Canada; would be pensionable in Canada; engaged when in and resident in Canada; the day of ceasing; the day engaged; undertaking given; form authorized.
#ASSERT `reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- (b)(ii): engaged not more than three months after the employee ceased to be employed abroad (10 January to 10 April).
#ASSERT `reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10)) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10)) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10)) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 11) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10)) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 9) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 16(2)(b)(ii) — the employee was engaged not more than three months after ceasing to be employed outside Canada` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 16(2)(b)(ii) — the employee was engaged not more than three months after ceasing to be employed outside Canada` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1))
